# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# The ONLY secret this project has. It is read exclusively inside app/api/**,
# never with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and never from the browser (CLAUDE.md §6).
#
# The app runs without it. Every route catches the missing-key error and serves
# its cached fixture with `degraded: true` rather than a 500, so all four
# screens still render — see samples/fallback-response.json. What you lose is
# the live audit parse, live skill extraction, and model-written schedule prose.
#
# GET /api/health returns { hasKey } if you want to confirm it is loaded, and
# it is worth checking on the deployed URL rather than locally: a missing env
# var in the Vercel dashboard is the most likely deploy mistake, precisely
# because .env.local never leaves the machine.
#
# `tsx` does NOT read this file — only `next dev` does. Offline scripts that
# need a key take it from the environment.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
